rev[ch[x][0]]\n        rev[ch[x][1]] = not rev[ch[x][1]]\n        rev[x] = False\n        ch[x][0], ch[x][1] = ch[x][1], ch[x][0]\n    if parity_rev[x]:\n        parity_rev[ch[x][0]] ^= 1\n        parity_rev[ch[x][1]] ^= 1\n        parity[ch[x][0]] ^= 1\n        parity[ch[x][1]] ^= 1\n        parity_rev[x] = 0\n\nPull:\n\ndef pull(x):\n    sz[x] = 1 + (sz[ch[x][0]] if ch[x][0]!=-1 else 0) + (sz[ch[x][1]] if ch[x][1]!=-1 else 0)\n    odd[x] = (odd[ch[x][0]] if ch[x][0]!=-1 else False) or (odd[ch[x][1]] if ch[x][1]!=-1 else False)\n\nNow need to maintain parity[x] correctly after rotations. Since we aren't adjusting parity on rotation, we need to ensure that after rotations, parity[x] still equals parity to root. Because rotations only change parent-child relationships but parity to root should remain same. Since we don't modify parity values during rotation, it's fine.\n\nNow implement rotate:\n\ndef rotate(x):\n    y = fa[x]\n    if fa[y] != -1:\n        ch[fa[y]][ch[fa[y]][1]==y] = x\n    fa[x] = fa[y]\n    ch[y][ch[y][0]==x] = x\n    fa[x] = y\n    # No parity adjustment needed\n    # Ensure children pointers correct\n    # After rotation, x becomes parent of y\n    # No further action\n\nNow splay:\n\ndef splay(x):\n    while fa[x] != -1:\n        y = fa[x]\n        z = fa[y]\n        if z != -1:\n            if (ch[y][0]==x) == (ch[z][0]==y):\n                rotate(y)\n            else:\n                rotate(x)\n        rotate(x)\n    pull(x)\n\nAccess:\n\ndef access(x):\n    y = 0\n    while True:\n        splay(x)\n        # make x the root of its tree\n        ch[x][1] = y\n        pull(x)\n        if y == 0:\n            break\n        y = fa[x]\n        fa[x] = -1\n        x = y\n\nEvert:\n\ndef evert(x):\n    access(x)\n    if fa[x] != -1:\n        rev[x] ^= True\n        push(x)\n\nNow we need to implement get_parity(u,v):\n\ndef get_parity(u, v):\n    if same(u, v):\n        return parity[u] ^ parity[v]\n    else:\n        return None\n\nNow main loop